{"id":176161745708003,"type":"artist","name":"Kula Shaker","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":16,"info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Kula_Shaker_-_Parkpop_2008.jpg?width=500","bio":"Kula Shaker nacieron a finales de los noventa en Inglaterra en plena tormenta brit pop, aunque lo suyo tuviera más que ver con el rock psicodélico y la mística de las bandas de los setenta.  Liderados por el carismático Crispian Mills, lograron auparse a lo más alto de las listas de ventas con Tattva, y vender más de un millón de copias de su álbum de debut, K (96), un tratado de rock clásico teñido de espiritualidad oriental.  Un éxito","tags":["britpop","Psychedelic Rock","indie","rock","alternative"]},"works":[{"id":179449699442528,"type":"song","name":"Hey Dude","artist":"Kula Shaker","year":1996,"weight":2,"yt":"KDHd-vxcMDo","src":"singles","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":248716836618435,"name":"Triple J Hottest 100 · 1996","rank":60,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":69225034879707,"type":"album","name":"K","artist":"Kula Shaker","year":1996,"weight":9,"yt":"736xS6vCK50","src":"books,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":242302941379922,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Britpop","rank":24,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":169744283793291,"type":"album","name":"Peasants, Pigs & Astronauts","artist":"Kula Shaker","year":1999,"weight":3,"yt":"7SRPmLtNvV0","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":242302941379922,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Britpop","rank":38,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":232868435203292,"type":"album","name":"Strangefolk","artist":"Kula Shaker","year":2007,"weight":3,"yt":"BGjymCNvwaY","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":242302941379922,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Britpop","rank":114,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":156430818035177,"type":"album","name":"Pilgrims Progress","artist":"Kula Shaker","year":2010,"weight":3,"yt":"P0B1_XsnUFU","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":242302941379922,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Britpop","rank":55,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":80274864358391,"type":"album","name":"1st Congregational Church of Eternal Love (And Free Hugs)","artist":"Kula Shaker","year":2022,"weight":3,"yt":"YJEfjN78rlE","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":242302941379922,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Britpop","rank":149,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":117823206903027,"type":"album","name":"Natural Magick","artist":"Kula Shaker","year":2024,"weight":3,"yt":"EE7tqWJhK74","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":242302941379922,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Britpop","rank":131,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":2636832073878,"type":"album","name":"Wormslayer","artist":"Kula Shaker","year":2026,"weight":3,"yt":"H9uO4hA3D1s","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":242302941379922,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Britpop","rank":117,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}}],"members":[],"member_of":[],"genres":[],"album_genres":[{"id":238796249276494,"type":"genre","name":"Britpop","n":7}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":62675748187365,"name":"Psicodelia británica de los noventa","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1989,"end":2002,"desc":"La edad de oro de la psicodelia británica no fueron los sesenta sino los noventa: las raves crean una demanda inagotable de música inducida por (o para) las drogas. La versión pop (Telescopes, Inspiral Carpets, Verve, Sundial, Auteurs, Kula Shaker), las más sofisticadas (Curve, Cranberries, Rollerskate Skinny, Beta Band, dEUS, Gorky's Zygotic Mynci), el space-rock libre (Porcupine Tree, Terminal Cheesecake, Heads), los últimos shoegazers (Ride, Swervedriver, Spectrum y E.A.R. de Sonic Boom, Spiritualized de Jason Pierce, Flying Saucer Attack, encuentro de shoegazing y ambient) y el dream-pop (Lush, Pale Saints, Slowdive, Catherine Wheel, Bark Psychosis).","color":"#c084fc","family":"Psicodelia, garage y shoegaze","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#brit-psych-90s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":69225034879707,"artist":"Kula Shaker","artist_id":176161745708003,"title":"K","year":1996,"ess":0,"yt":"736xS6vCK50","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Psicodelia británica de los noventa","scene_id":62675748187365,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#brit-psych-90s","chapters":["Sección 6.3"],"pages":[[1,239,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":239,"text":"…New Wave (1993), a nostalgic tribute to the hippie era; Whipping Boy's Heartworm (1995), in Ireland, a work drenched in neoclassical melancholy; Kula Shaker's derivative but exuberant K (1996). Plus Jellyfish Kiss, the Dylans, Jack, Freed Unit, etc etc. What was truly remarkable about these bands is how…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Similar to Oasis","body":"Kula Shaker was among the bands that started to appear, sounding similar to Oasis, demonstrating the latter's popularity and influence within the Britpop scene. \"The Oasis approach proved to be so popular that they started to hear and see similar bands.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of Alt Rock: Chapter 12","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DSvoppf1dGY"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":69225034879707,"type":"album","name":"K","list_id":242302941379922,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Britpop","src":"musthear","rank":24,"year":1996,"note":null,"yt":"736xS6vCK50","scaruffi":null},{"id":179449699442528,"type":"song","name":"Hey Dude","work_year":1996,"list_id":248716836618435,"list":"Triple J Hottest 100 ·